1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:03,835
The value of intelligence is not just about
doing calculations.

2
00:00:03,875 --> 00:00:06,500
Learning, remembering, changing through
experience,

3
00:00:06,500 --> 00:00:08,765
and using what has been learned also
matter.

4
00:00:08,805 --> 00:00:14,025
DEE investigates these capabilities through
a three-dimensional computational universe.

5
00:00:14,065 --> 00:00:19,260
We will explore mechanisms that its
research has already put into operation.

6
00:00:20,350 --> 00:00:23,500
In a trained neural network, learning can
involve

7
00:00:23,500 --> 00:00:26,200
adjusting the strength of its connections.

8
00:00:26,240 --> 00:00:31,535
In DEE, the mechanism we will observe is
different: elements move, meet,

9
00:00:31,535 --> 00:00:35,285
and transform their organization under
fixed rules.

10
00:00:35,325 --> 00:00:40,666
The computer executes those rules;
experience changes the internal conditions

11
00:00:40,666 --> 00:00:42,885
that contribute to the response.

12
00:00:44,350 --> 00:00:48,285
An experience leaves a relationship that
can contribute again later.

13
00:00:48,325 --> 00:00:53,560
In this test, two inputs meet and form a
transformation relationship.

14
00:00:53,600 --> 00:00:58,665
Later, a different signal arrives: when it
encounters what was learned, it changes.

15
00:00:58,705 --> 00:01:02,990
The system thus uses a previous experience
with a new input.

16
00:01:03,030 --> 00:01:09,590
We call this learning: experience changes
how subsequent inputs are processed.

17
00:01:16,350 --> 00:01:18,770
Learning also includes revision.

18
00:01:18,835 --> 00:01:22,120
First, a signal activates an acquired
relationship.

19
00:01:22,160 --> 00:01:25,105
Then a different experience is presented.

20
00:01:25,230 --> 00:01:29,870
The same signal enters again, but now it
encounters a changed organization and

21
00:01:29,870 --> 00:01:31,655
produces a different response.

22
00:01:31,695 --> 00:01:35,500
This is plasticity: changing an existing
relationship.

23
00:01:35,540 --> 00:01:39,675
Other associations can remain available
while this one is revised.

24
00:01:39,715 --> 00:01:43,047
The difference lies in the system's
history;

25
00:01:43,047 --> 00:01:45,925
its fundamental rules remain the same.

26
00:01:48,350 --> 00:01:51,510
Remembering means that this history becomes
useful again.

27
00:01:51,550 --> 00:01:56,986
DEE has shown relationships retained in
carriers, differences between components,

28
00:01:56,986 --> 00:01:59,000
and distributed organizations.

29
00:01:59,040 --> 00:02:03,475
Some functions remain available after other
activities and a waiting period.

30
00:02:03,515 --> 00:02:06,761
And when a complete trajectory is saved and
reopened,

31
00:02:06,761 --> 00:02:09,210
it can continue using what was acquired.

32
00:02:10,350 --> 00:02:13,410
Learned relationships can also be combined.

33
00:02:13,450 --> 00:02:16,762
Here, a query passes through two successive
encounters:

34
00:02:16,762 --> 00:02:21,580
the first relationship transforms the
signal, and its result reaches the second.

35
00:02:21,620 --> 00:02:24,230
The point is not the number thirty.

36
00:02:24,270 --> 00:02:27,602
It is that two earlier experiences
contribute

37
00:02:27,602 --> 00:02:30,785
to a processing chain within the DEE world.

38
00:02:30,825 --> 00:02:36,845
Other experiments show that the order of
interactions can also change the result.

39
00:02:38,350 --> 00:02:41,665
Information can also travel between
organizations.

40
00:02:41,705 --> 00:02:44,221
One participant receives an experience;

41
00:02:44,221 --> 00:02:48,350
a material message reaches another and
changes a later response.

42
00:02:48,405 --> 00:02:53,165
In other tests, a query makes it possible
to receive missing information and use it.

43
00:02:53,205 --> 00:02:55,719
Communication therefore has a consequence:

44
00:02:55,719 --> 00:02:59,370
what happens in one place contributes to
what another can do.

45
00:03:00,350 --> 00:03:03,860
Transfer means moving an acquired function
to another support,

46
00:03:03,860 --> 00:03:06,465
or using an experience in a different
context.

47
00:03:06,505 --> 00:03:10,560
DEE has demonstrated both possibilities in
different experiments.

48
00:03:10,600 --> 00:03:12,949
Communication routes have also been
protected,

49
00:03:12,949 --> 00:03:15,910
and useful functions recovered through
prepared resources.

50
00:03:15,950 --> 00:03:19,832
The technological value lies in preserving
and reusing functions,

51
00:03:19,832 --> 00:03:21,385
as well as acquiring them.

52
00:03:22,350 --> 00:03:26,110
Using a memory depends on how it is
accessed.

53
00:03:26,150 --> 00:03:29,591
Previously acquired content has been
recovered by changing the access route,

54
00:03:29,591 --> 00:03:31,175
without teaching the content again.

55
00:03:31,215 --> 00:03:36,890
A real emission missed by the usual reader
could be read at another moment and used.

56
00:03:36,930 --> 00:03:40,915
We also confirmed that introducing a probe
can change the world.

57
00:03:40,955 --> 00:03:46,900
We therefore study information, access, and
the effect of observation together.

58
00:03:50,350 --> 00:03:55,123
Experience has also enabled anticipation of
an event before it occurs,

59
00:03:55,123 --> 00:03:56,760
within tested sequences.

60
00:03:56,800 --> 00:03:59,430
Other mechanisms link action, consequence,

61
00:03:59,430 --> 00:04:02,560
and subsequent change through their own
evolution.

62
00:04:02,600 --> 00:04:05,628
Time and order are part of the processing:

63
00:04:05,628 --> 00:04:09,305
what happened earlier changes what can
happen next.

64
00:04:10,350 --> 00:04:13,386
When a consequence returns to the system,

65
00:04:13,386 --> 00:04:16,940
it can change a reference and a later
selection.

66
00:04:16,980 --> 00:04:22,590
Adaptation experiments showed useful
actions that depended on this experience.

67
00:04:22,630 --> 00:04:27,297
DEE outputs have also been connected to
environments and tools:

68
00:04:27,297 --> 00:04:32,705
an emission can produce an action, and its
effect can become a new input.

69
00:04:34,350 --> 00:04:38,140
The landscape can receive and combine many
contributions.

70
00:04:38,180 --> 00:04:42,145
One experimental family integrated one
hundred and twenty-eight components,

71
00:04:42,145 --> 00:04:44,260
testing the effect of changing each one.

72
00:04:44,300 --> 00:04:48,769
In another trajectory, memory and
comparison were used successively and

73
00:04:48,769 --> 00:04:50,595
during overlapping intervals.

74
00:04:50,635 --> 00:04:56,502
We can thus study several activities in one
world and observe how resources,

75
00:04:56,502 --> 00:04:59,435
encounters, and timing influence them.

76
00:05:00,350 --> 00:05:03,860
Words can also act as access signals.

77
00:05:03,900 --> 00:05:06,918
A learned association can enable the use of
a function,

78
00:05:06,918 --> 00:05:10,320
and a revision can change which access is
activated afterward.

79
00:05:10,360 --> 00:05:14,894
In a recent test, revising what was learned
about a signal changed which function

80
00:05:14,894 --> 00:05:17,245
was queried through a prepared connection.

81
00:05:17,285 --> 00:05:21,380
The acquired experience had a concrete
functional consequence.

82
00:05:22,350 --> 00:05:25,015
These mechanisms have also been used
together.

83
00:05:25,055 --> 00:05:29,072
Some trajectories combine new associations,
earlier memories, queries,

84
00:05:29,072 --> 00:05:30,335
and connected actions.

85
00:05:30,375 --> 00:05:33,768
Others combine memory, comparison, and
numerical operations,

86
00:05:33,768 --> 00:05:36,370
using the result of one operation in the
next.

87
00:05:36,410 --> 00:05:41,205
Complete states can be saved and reopened
to continue the same history.

88
00:05:42,350 --> 00:05:45,980
DEE brings together an engine, tools, and
organizations with history.

89
00:05:46,020 --> 00:05:48,043
Its value lies in this diversity of
mechanisms

90
00:05:48,043 --> 00:05:49,890
and in how they can relate to one another.

91
00:05:49,930 --> 00:05:52,123
This foundation opens development paths for

92
00:05:52,123 --> 00:05:54,570
adaptive systems and assistants with
continuity.

93
00:05:54,610 --> 00:05:59,300
From Puebla, we seek collaboration to
develop and evaluate these possibilities.
